hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"175","On the authority of Ahmad bin Abdah, on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Musa bin Salim Abi Jahdam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaidullah bin Abbas, who said: We were sitting with Ibn Abbas, and he said: “By God, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not single us out for anything other than the people except three things: He commanded us That we perform ablution properly, that we do not eat charity, and that we do not ride donkeys over horses.” Yaqoub Al-Dawraqi told us, Ibn Ulayya told us, Musa bin Salem told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid Allah bin Abbas, he said: Ibn Abbas said The same, and more. Musa said: I met Abdullah bin Hassan, and I said: Abdullah bin Ubaid Allah told me such-and-such, and he said: The horses were among my children. Hashem was few, so he wanted to multiply them."
"176","Ibn Abi Safwan Muhammad bin Othman Al-Thaqafi told us, my father told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah, and he is Ibn Masoud, on the authority of his father, said: “A deal for both deals is usury, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to perform ablution completely.”"
